# Lecture 10C

## Set #5: Medicinal Biotechnology
## Chapters 17-19
## Dr. Neil Voss
## Nov 5, 2026

=== layout: bookend

# Learning Objectives

@body

- Explain how a therapeutic payload, vector, route, and target tissue work together.
- Compare genome-editing strategies and the safety questions that limit each one.
- Connect stem-cell and cancer biotechnology to evidence, delivery, and clinical decisions.

=== layout: definitions

# A Few Useful Words

@body

- Payload: the DNA, RNA, protein, or cells that a treatment must deliver.
- Vector: a carrier used to get genetic material into a cell.
- Transgene: a gene introduced into a cell by genetic engineering.
- Episome: DNA maintained outside the cell's chromosomes.

